menu "Log capture"

    config LOG_CAPTURE_SIZE_KB
        int "Boot-log ring buffer size (KiB, PSRAM)"
        default 256 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
        default 1024
        range 32 4096
        help
            Every ESP_LOG line is mirrored into this PSRAM ring so the Logs
            screen and the companion app can show the boot log after the fact.
            Allocated once at the very start of app_main and never freed.

            1 MiB is comfortable on the P4 boards (32 MiB PSRAM). The ESP32-S3
            board has 8 MiB total and spends 0.9 MiB of it on the two LCD frame
            buffers plus up to ~3 MiB on an OTA image being staged, so it takes
            a quarter of that.

endmenu
